/godotengine/godot/pull/113152.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113152.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"- Follow-up of #111967 \r\n\r\nAfter #111967, `cast_to` cannot be \"naively\" called anymore because it has a second template parameter.\r\nImplementing it this way was a practical decision, to make the change a bit simpler, to make #111967 easier to merge.\r\n\r\nIn the new PR, `derives_from` is shadowed for every `Object` subclass. Right now, shadowing it is only used to statically protect against mistakes. Theoretically, it could be used to optimize the cast in certain cases, but this is unlikely to matter.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113152/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113152/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}